[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "2607252800"
  :adr/title "Capability WIT v2.1 requires explicit named grant acquisition"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-25"
  :adr/supersedes ["2607252700"]
  :adr/body "# Explicit grant acquisition\n\n## Decision\n\nThe first v2 grant ABI could issue only one unspecified grant from `capability.acquire()`. That shape is safe only when an admitted Component has one effect, and it prevents safe multi-effect Components.\n\n`aiueos:capability@0.3.0` replaces it with `acquire(request: grant-request)`. `grant-request` is a closed enum covering the seven named operations. The request is a routing label, never a descriptor or an authority token. A host MUST issue a grant only when its admitted immutable descriptor contains the exact requested operation, and MUST bind the returned resource to that operation.\n\nThe native host MUST reject a borrowed grant at every provider interface whose operation differs from the grant's binding. Thus a guest may request `clock-now` while being admitted for `http-post`, but receives a denial; it cannot select or widen a new capability.\n\n## Consequences\n\nThis is a breaking WIT change and is published as package version `0.3.0`. No v2.0 Component may be silently reinterpreted. Compiler and native linker conformance must include both an unadmitted request denial and a two-operation Component whose grants cannot cross interfaces."}]
